url: "https://github.com/ANR-MAMUT/MAMUT-routing-Mamut2026"
abstract: >-
  Mamut2026 is an original CVRP benchmark proposed by the listed authors to study solver performance across Euclidean distance, road distance and free-flow travel-time metrics. Instances are generated on OpenStreetMap city networks, with controlled demand distributions, route-size bands, depot and customer placements, and customer-sourcing methods. Candidate generation and diversity-based selection produce a collection spanning instance characteristics, with 3 metric variants over each shared base. Its design adapts the instance-design vocabulary of the Uchoa et al. (2017) X set to real road networks. Geographic data are credited to OpenStreetMap and its contributors.
